y", "rel.occupies"], "params": ["p.zone_entry_wait_reach", "p.halt_speed_tolerance"], "convention": "queueing at a curb space: a stop interferes with a bus or taxicab where, at some observation of the stop so far, it stands halted outside the zone within one passenger-car length plus a queue spacing of it (p.zone_entry_wait_reach), the place a vehicle waits to take the space", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) whose footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) a curb zone z (st.curb_zone) that is of kind bus_stop while the subject is not a bus (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-030::bus false), or of kind taxicab_stand while the subject is not a taxicab (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-270::taxicab false).", "obligation": "Wherever the subject occupies such a zone z (selected again as in the applicability, with its kind and the subject's class), the subject is not halted (drv.motion.complete_halt with p.halt_speed_tolerance), except a halt that is (a) to avoid conflict with other traffic: some other road user is ahead of the subject in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) with a gap between bodies (rel.surface_gap) at most p.queue_halt_gap; or (b) in compliance with a device or an officer: a travel region the subject occupies is governed (dev.governs) by a stop sign, a yield sign, a traffic signal displaying a red or yellow indication or flashing_red, a railway signal or gate with lights flashing or gate not up, or a person in the role police_officer giving the indication stop; or (c) a temporary, expeditious stop of a passenger vehicle for passengers: the subject is neither a truck (ru.truck) nor a trailer or combination (ru.trailer_or_combination), it is not parked with min_duration p.standing_min_duration (drv.motion.parked), a door of the subject is open (sig.door_open) at some observation of the same halt, before or after the observation, and at no observation of the halt up to the judged one is there a road user other than the subject that is a bus or a taxicab (the two admitted aggregates), whose footprint does not overlap z, which is halted (drv.motion.complete_halt), and whose body's ground distance to z (st.region_geometry) is at most p.zone_entry_wait_reach.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance", "p.queue_halt_gap", "p.standing_min_duration", "p.zone_entry_wait_reach"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "'A person shall not stop, stand or park a vehicle' is read on the vehicle's controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s7", "why": "'The driver of a passenger vehicle' is read on the vehicle's controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s6", "why": "Official designation and appropriate signing are read from the presence of the curb zone of kind bus_stop or taxicab_stand on the road.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s7", "why": "'Passenger vehicle', which no posted definition defines, is read as a vehicle that is neither a truck nor a trailer or combination.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "s9", "why": "The purpose of loading or unloading passengers is read by a door of the halted vehicle open during the halt.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "purpose"}, {"span": "s14", "why": "'Waiting to enter or about to enter' is read by a bus or taxicab halted outside the zone within the waiting reach; one still moving toward the zone is not read as waiting.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "intention"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A passenger car halts in a bus_stop curb zone for longer than the standing duration, doors closed; no road user ahead and no stop control governs its lane."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A passenger car halts briefly in a bus_stop curb zone with its curb-side door open and moves off before the standing duration; no other road user is in the scene."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A bus halts in a bus_stop curb zone."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "A passenger car halts briefly in a taxicab_stand curb zone and the source does not observe its doors.", "masked": ["sig.door_open"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A passenger car halts briefly in a bus_stop zone with a door open while a bus stands halted just outside the zone within the waiting reach."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A truck halts briefly in a taxicab_stand zone with a door open: it is no passenger vehicle."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition source (sensor or simulator specification)"}, {"name": "p.queue_halt_gap", "unit": "m", "value": 5.0, "convention": "the gap between bodies to a road user ahead in the same lane within which a halt is a halt behind other traffic: the spacing of halted vehicles in a queue", "source": "HCM queue spacing of stopped vehicles"}, {"name": "p.standing_min_duration", "unit": "s", "value": 60.0, "convention": "the longest halt counted as receiving or discharging passengers or loading rather than standing: a passenger pick-up dwell at the curb", "source": "curbside passenger pick-up dwell observations (ITE curbside management practice)"}, {"name": "p.zone_entry_wait_reach", "unit": "m", "value": 10.0, "convention": "the ground distance from a halted vehicle's body to a curb zone within which the vehicle counts as waiting to enter the zone: about one design passenger-car length plus the spacing of halted vehicles 