, "st.curb_zone"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Freight curb loading zone' is 'a space adjacent to a curb for the exclusive use of vehicles during the loading or unloading of freight' (DEF-NRS-484B-023): st.curb_zone of kind freight_loading, 'a signed or marked length of curb', which the subject's footprint overlaps (rel.occupies). The marking is the evidence of the designation."}, {"span": "s6", "atoms": ["dev.zone_sign", "dev.governs", "prim.conditions_hold", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "The hours of the zone are those its posting states: a zone sign of kind parking_restricted (dev.zone_sign, with its 'conditions attribute ... a list of time windows'; an unrestricted legend is 'the empty set (unconditional)') governing (dev.governs) a travel region (st.travel_region) the subject occupies (rel.occupies); whether its hours hold now is prim.conditions_hold, never the sign itself (dev.zone_sign is 'not a stand-in for whether the condition holds now')."}, {"span": "s7", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Driver' is 'every person who drives or is in actual physical control of a vehicle' (DEF-NRS-484A-080): a role, read through the vehicle's controlled motion; 'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle. The driver is the subject's own vehicle."}, {"span": "s9", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.curb_zone"], "derived": [], "justification": "The same freight_loading curb zone (st.curb_zone, 'a signed or marked length of curb') the subject's footprint overlaps (rel.occupies), re-bound with the selection of s5."}, {"span": "s10", "atoms": ["sig.door_open"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "The purpose and engagement 'in loading or unloading passengers' are read by the conduct: a door of the halted vehicle (drv.motion.complete_halt) open (sig.door_open, 'a door open') during the halt, the act through which passengers board or alight."}, {"span": "s12", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle", "ru.truck"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Motor vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle ('every vehicle which is self-propelled but not operated upon rails'); a motor vehicle 'used for the transportation of materials' is the class whose contract is exactly that: ru.truck, 'motor vehicle for carrying goods, with a body built for that purpose', carried beside the aggregate, not in place of it."}, {"span": "s13", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.curb_zone", "st.region_geometry"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "'Waiting to enter or about to enter such zone' is read by the conduct: the goods vehicle does not overlap the zone (rel.occupies, st.curb_zone of kind freight_loading, the zone of s5) and is halted (drv.motion.complete_halt) with the ground distance from its body to the zone (st.region_geometry, 'the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it') within p.zone_entry_wait_reach. The relation is the distance the words imply ('waiting to enter'), not a belonging."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "s3", "standard": "expeditious", "concepts": ["drv.motion.parked"], "params": ["p.commercial_loading_max_halt", "p.halt_speed_tolerance"], "convention": "commercial loading zone time limit: a halt counts as expeditious loading or unloading of materials while it has not lasted as long as the thirty-minute limit common to commercial loading zones, i.e. while the subject is not at rest at every observation of a window of length p.commercial_loading_max_halt behind the observation (drv.motion.parked)", "surrogate": false}, {"span": "s8", "standard": "temporarily", "concepts": ["drv.motion.parked"], "params": ["p.standing_min_duration", "p.halt_speed_tolerance"], "convention": "curbside passenger pick-up dwell: a stop counts as temporary while it has not lasted as long as a passenger pick-up dwell, i.e. while the subject is not at rest at every observation of a window of length p.standing_min_duration behind the observation (drv.motion.parked)", "surrogate": false}, {"span": "s11", "standard": "does not interfere with", "concepts": ["drv.motion.complete_halt", "st.region_geometry", "rel.occupies"], "params": ["p.zone_entry_wait_reach", "p.halt_speed_tolerance"], "convention": "queueing at a curb space: a stop interferes with a goods vehicle where, at some observation of the stop so far, that vehicle stands halted outside the zone within one passenger-car length plus a queue spacing of it (p.zone_entry_wait_reach), the place a vehicle waits to take the space", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [{"span": "s2", "why": "'For any purpose or length of time' excludes no halt: every halt is within the prohibition whatever its purpose and length, so the duty is the same whether or not these words are read.", "scope": "none"}], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) whose footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) a curb zone z of kind freight_loading (st.curb_zone), and the zone's provisions are in effect: every zone sign of kind parking_restricted (dev.zone_sign) that governs (dev.governs) a travel region (st.travel_region) the subject occupies has its conditions holding for the subject (prim.conditions_hold); where no such sign governs, the marked zone is read as in effect at all hours.", "obligation": "Wherever the subject occupies such a zone z in effect (selected again as in the applicability), the subject is not halted (drv.motion.complete_halt with p.halt_speed_tolerance), except a halt that is (a) to avoid conflict with other traffic: some other road user is ahead of the subject in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) with a gap between bodies (rel.surface_gap) at most p.queue_halt_gap; or (b) in compliance with 