 at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition source (sensor or simulator specification)"}, {"name": "p.queue_halt_gap", "unit": "m", "value": 5.0, "convention": "the gap between bodies to a road user ahead in the same lane within which a halt is a halt behind other traffic: the spacing of halted vehicles in a queue", "source": "HCM queue spacing of stopped vehicles"}, {"name": "p.commercial_loading_max_halt", "unit": "s", "value": 1800.0, "convention": "the longest halt of a commercial vehicle counted as expeditious loading or unloading of goods or passengers: the thirty-minute limit common to commercial loading zones", "source": "municipal commercial loading zone time limits"}, {"name": "p.standing_min_duration", "unit": "s", "value": 60.0, "convention": "the longest halt counted as receiving or discharging passengers or loading rather than standing: a passenger pick-up dwell at the curb", "source": "curbside passenger pick-up dwell observations (ITE curbside management practice)"}, {"name": "p.zone_entry_wait_reach", "unit": "m", "value": 10.0, "convention": "the ground distance from a halted vehicle's body to a curb zone within which the vehicle counts as waiting to enter the zone: about one design passenger-car length plus the spacing of halted vehicles in a queue", "source": "AASHTO Green Book design vehicle dimensions; HCM queue spacing"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
