ception.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "purpose"}, {"span": "s10", "why": "The purpose of and engagement in loading or unloading passengers are read by a door of the halted vehicle open during the halt.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "purpose"}, {"span": "s13", "why": "'Waiting to enter or about to enter' is read by the conduct it leads to: a goods vehicle halted outside the zone within the waiting reach of it; one still moving toward the zone is not read as waiting.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "intention"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "'Marked as' a freight curb loading zone is read from the presence of the curb zone of that kind.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A passenger car halts inside a freight_loading curb zone that no sign governs, for longer than the standing duration, doors closed; no road user ahead and no stop control governs its lane."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A truck halts in the zone with its curb-side door open and moves off before the commercial loading duration has elapsed."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A passenger car halts at a curb where there is no curb zone."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "A passenger car halts in the zone briefly, shorter than the standing duration, and the source does not observe its doors.", "masked": ["sig.door_open"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A passenger car halts briefly in the zone with a door open while a truck stands halted just outside the zone, within the waiting reach of it."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A passenger car halts briefly in the zone with a door open; no other road user is in the scene."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition source (sensor or simulator specification)"}, {"name": "p.queue_halt_gap", "unit": "m", "value": 5.0, "convention": "the gap between bodies to a road user ahead in the same lane within which a halt is a halt behind other traffic: the spacing of halted vehicles in a queue", "source": "HCM queue spacing of stopped vehicles"}, {"name": "p.commercial_loading_max_halt", "unit": "s", "value": 1800.0, "convention": "the longest halt of a commercial vehicle counted as expeditious loading or unloading of goods or passengers: the thirty-minute limit common to commercial loading zones", "source": "municipal commercial loading zone time limits"}, {"name": "p.standing_min_duration", "unit": "s", "value": 60.0, "convention": "the longest halt counted as receiving or discharging passengers or loading rather than standing: a passenger pick-up dwell at the curb", "source": "curbside passenger pick-up dwell observations (ITE curbside management practice)"}, {"name": "p.zone_entry_wait_reach", "unit": "m", "value": 10.0, "convention": "the ground distance from a halted vehicle's body to a curb zone within which the vehicle counts as waiting to enter the zone: about one design passenger-car length plus the spacing of halted vehicles in a queue", "source": "AASHTO Green Book design vehicle dimensions; HCM queue spacing"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_510", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-510"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "A person shall not stop, stand or park a vehicle", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "for any purpose or length of time", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "in any restricted parking zone", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "other than for the purpose to which parking in such zone is restricted,", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "except that a driver of a passenger vehicle", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s6", "text": "may stop temporarily", "role": "standard"}, {"id": "s7", "text": "in such zone", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s8", "text": "for the purpose of and while actually engaged in loading or unloading of passengers", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s9", "text": "when such stopping does not interfere with", "role": "standard"}, {"id": "s10", "text": "any vehicle which is waiting to enter or about to enter the zone", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s11", "text": "for the purpose of parking in accordance with the purpose to which parking is restricted.", "role": "exception"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["dev.governs", "dev.human_direction", "dev.railway_signal_or_gate", "dev.stop_sign", "dev.traffic_signal", "dev.yield_sign", "rel.ahead_behind_in_lane", "rel.occupies", "rel.surface_gap", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "st.travel_region"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "'Stop' when prohibited is 'any halting, even momentarily, of a vehicle, whether occupied or not, except when necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic or in compliance with the directions of a police officer or official traffic-control device' (DEF-NRS-484A-260, the definition the table resolves for 'stopping' in this law); 'stand' is 'the halting of a vehicle, whether occupied or not' (DEF-NRS-484A-250) and 'park' 'th