an": "s5", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "ru.truck", "ru.trailer_or_combination"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Driver' is 'every person who drives or is in actual physical control of a vehicle' (DEF-NRS-484A-080), read through the vehicle's controlled motion. 'Passenger vehicle' has no posted definition: it is read as a vehicle (the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) not built to carry goods or to be drawn: not ru.truck ('motor vehicle for carrying goods, with a body built for that purpose') and not ru.trailer_or_combination ('vehicle drawn by another, or the combination'). The class atoms are carried beside the aggregate, never in place of it."}, {"span": "s7", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.curb_zone"], "derived": [], "justification": "'In such zone': the same restricted_parking curb zone (st.curb_zone) the subject's footprint overlaps (rel.occupies), re-bound with the selection of s3."}, {"span": "s8", "atoms": ["sig.door_open"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "The purpose of and engagement 'in loading or unloading of passengers' are read by the conduct: a door of the halted vehicle (drv.motion.complete_halt) open (sig.door_open, 'a door open') during the halt."}, {"span": "s10", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "rel.occupies", "st.curb_zone", "st.region_geometry"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "'Any vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; 'waiting to enter or about to enter the zone' is read by the conduct: that vehicle does not overlap the zone (rel.occupies, st.curb_zone of s3) and is halted (drv.motion.complete_halt) with the ground distance from its body to the zone (st.region_geometry, 'the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it') within p.zone_entry_wait_reach."}, {"span": "s11", "atoms": ["prim.conditions_hold", "dev.zone_sign", "dev.governs", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "Parking 'in accordance with the purpose to which parking is restricted' is read, for the waiting vehicle, as the conditions of the parking_restricted zone sign (dev.zone_sign) governing (dev.governs) a travel region (st.travel_region) the subject occupies holding for that vehicle (prim.conditions_hold, 'any occupancy or class condition is met')."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "s6", "standard": "temporarily", "concepts": ["drv.motion.parked"], "params": ["p.standing_min_duration", "p.halt_speed_tolerance"], "convention": "curbside passenger pick-up dwell: a stop counts as temporary while it has not lasted as long as a passenger pick-up dwell, i.e. while the subject is not at rest at every observation of a window of length p.standing_min_duration behind the observation (drv.motion.parked)", "surrogate": false}, {"span": "s9", "standard": "does not interfere with", "concepts": ["drv.motion.complete_halt", "st.region_geometry", "rel.occupies"], "params": ["p.zone_entry_wait_reach", "p.halt_speed_tolerance"], "convention": "queueing at a curb space: a stop interferes with a vehicle where, at some observation of the stop so far, that vehicle stands halted outside the zone within one passenger-car length plus a queue spacing of it (p.zone_entry_wait_reach), the place a vehicle waits to take the space", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [{"span": "s2", "why": "'For any purpose or length of time' excludes no halt: every halt is within the prohibition whatever its purpose and length, so the duty is the same whether or not these words are read.", "scope": "none"}], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) whose footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) a curb zone z of kind restricted_parking (st.curb_zone).", "obligation": "Wherever the subject occupies such a zone z (selected again as in the applicability), the subject is not halted (drv.motion.complete_halt with p.halt_speed_tolerance), except a halt that is (a) to avoid conflict with other traffic: some other road user is ahead of the subject in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) with a gap between bodies (rel.surface_gap) at most p.queue_halt_gap; or (b) in compliance with a device or an officer: a travel region the subject occupies is governed (dev.governs) by a stop sign, a yield sign, a traffic signal displaying a red or yellow indication or flashing_red, a railway signal or gate with lights flashing or gate not up, or a person in the role police_officer giving the indication stop; or (c) for the purpose to which parking is restricted: some zone sign of kind parking_restricted (dev.zone_sign) governing (dev.governs) a travel region the subject occupies has its conditions holding for the subject (prim.conditions_hold); or (d) a temporary stop of a passenger vehicle for passengers: the subject is neither a truck (ru.truck) nor a trailer or combination (ru.trailer_or_combination), it is not parked with min_duration p.standing_min_duration (drv.motion.parked), a door of the subject is open (sig.door_open) at some observation of the same halt, before or after the observation, and at no observation of the halt up to the judged one is there a vehicle other than the subject (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) whose footprint does not overlap z, which is halted (drv.motion.complete_halt), whose body's ground distance to z (st.region_geometry) is at most p.zone_entry_wait_reach, and for which the conditions of such a parking_restricted zone sign hold (prim.conditions_hold).", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance", "p.queue_halt_gap", "p.standing_min_duration", "p.zone_entry_wait_reach"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "'A person shall not stop, stand or park a vehicle' is read on the vehicle's controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "'A driver of a passenger vehicle' is read on the vehicle's controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s4", "why": "The purpose of a halt is read through the class, occupancy and time conditions of the zone's posted sign holding for the vehicle; a restriction to a purpose the sign's legend states as none of these is not read, and a halt outside the sign's posted hours is read as not for the restricted purpose.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "purpose"}, {"span": "s8", "why": "The purpose of and engagement in loading or unloading passengers are read by a door of the halted vehicle open during the halt.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "purpose"}, {"span": "s10", "why": "'Waiting to enter or about to enter' is read by a vehicle halted outside the zone within the waiting reach; one still moving toward the zone is not read as waiting.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "intention"}, {"span": "s11", "why": "The waiting vehicle's purpose of parking in accordance with the restriction is read by the posted sign's conditions holding for it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "purpose"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A passenger car halts in a restricted_parking curb zone, governed by a parking_restricted zone sign whose class condition the car does not meet, for longer than the standing duration, doors closed."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A vehicle meeting the sign's class condition, at a time inside its posted hours, parks in the zone."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A passenger car halts at a curb where there is no restricted_parking curb zone."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "A passenger car not meeting the sign's conditions halts briefly in the zone, shorter than the standing duration; the source does not observe its doors.", "masked": ["sig.door_open"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A passenger car not meeting the sign's conditions halts briefly with a door open; no other road user is in the scene."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A passenger car halts briefly with a door open while a vehicle meeting the sign's conditions stands halted just outside the zone within the waiting reach."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition source (sensor or simulator specification)"}, {"name": "p.queue_halt_gap", "unit": "m", "value": 5.0, "convention": "the gap between bodies to a road user ahead in the same lane within which a halt is a halt behind other traffic: the spacing of halted vehicles in a queue", "source": "HCM queue spacing of stopped vehicles"}, {"name": "p.standing_min_duration", "unit": "s", "value": 60.0, "convention": "the longest halt counted as receiving or discharging passengers or loading rather than standing: a passenger pick-up dwell at the curb", "source": "curbside passenger pick-up dwell observations (ITE curbside management practice)"}, {"name": "p.zone_entry_wait_reach", "unit": "m", "value": 10.0, "convention": "the ground distance from a halted vehicle's body to a curb zone within which the vehicle counts as waiting to enter the zone: about one design passenger-car length plus the spacing of halted vehicles in a queue", "source": "AASHTO Green Book design vehicle dimensions; HCM queue spacing"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_517", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-517"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "A person shall not stop, stand or park a vehicle", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "other than a bus", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "in a bus stop,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "or a taxicab", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "in a taxicab stand,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s6", "text": "when such stop or stand has been officially designated and appropriately signed,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s7", "text": "except that the driver of a passenger vehicle", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s8", "text": "may temporarily stop there", "role": "standard"}, {"id": "s9", "text": "and for the purpose of and while actually engaged in", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s10", "text": "expeditiously", "role": "standard"}, {"id": "s11", "text": "loading or unloading of passengers", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s12", "text": "when such stopping does not interfere with", "role": "standard"}, {"id": "s13", "text": "any bus or taxicab", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s14", "text": "waiting to enter or about to enter such zone.", "role": "exception"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["dev.governs", "dev.human_direction", "dev.railway_signal_or_gate", "dev.stop_sign", "dev.traffic_signal", "dev.yield_sign", "rel.ahead_behind_in_lane", "rel.occupies", "rel.surface_gap", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "st.travel_region"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "'Stop' when prohibited is 'any halting, even momentarily, of a vehicle, whether occupied or not, except when necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic or in compliance with the directions of a police officer or official traffic-control device' (DEF-NRS-484A-260, the definition the table resolves for 'stopping' in this law); 'stand' is 'the halting of a vehicle, whether occupied or not' (DEF-NRS-484A-250) and 'park' 'the standing of a vehicle' (DEF-NRS-484A-155): together a halt, drv.motion.complete_halt ('at rest at the observation ... its speed at or below a tolerance', p.halt_speed_tolerance). The definition's exclusions are carried beside it: a halt with another road user ahead in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) within p.queue_halt_gap of the body (rel.surface_gap, 'distance between the nearest points of two bodies', not a centre distance) avoids conflict with other traffic; a halt on a travel region the subject occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region) governed (dev.governs) by a stop sign, a yield sign, a traffic signal showing red or yellow, a railway signal flashing or a gate not up, or a police officer's stop indication (dev.stop_sign, dev.yield_sign, dev.traffic_signal, dev.railway_signal_or_gate, dev.human_direction) complies with a device or an officer. 'Vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-030::bus"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Bus' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-030::bus ('a vehicle owned by the State, a political subdivision or a private school or nursery, designed for carrying ... passengers and used for the transportation of persons, or a vehicle, other than a taxicab, designed and used for the transportation of persons for compensation'), claimed as one atom, never expanded."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.curb_zone"], "derived": [], "justification": "A bus stop at the curb is st.curb_zone of kind bus_stop ('a signed or marked length of curb'), which the subject's footprint overlaps (rel.occupies, 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region (... curb zone ...)')."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-270::taxicab"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Taxicab' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-270::taxicab ('a motor vehicle designed or constructed to accommodate and transport ... passengers, including the driver, and used to transport passengers for a charge or fee'), claimed as one atom."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.curb_zone"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Taxicab stand' is 'a fixed area in a highway parallel and adjacent to the curb or edge of the highway and set aside for taxicabs to stand for passengers' (DEF-NRS-484B-067): st.curb_zone of kind taxicab_stand ('a signed or marked length of curb'), which the subject's footprint overlaps (rel.occupies)."}, {"span": "s6", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.curb_zone"], "derived": [], "justification": "That the stop or stand 'has been officially designated and appropriately signed' is its legal status, read from the feature's presence on the road: the curb zone of kind bus_stop or taxicab_stand the subject occupies (st.curb_zone, 'a signed or marked length of curb'; rel.occupies) is presumed designated and signed."}, {"span": "s7", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "ru.truck", "ru.trailer_or_combination"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Driver' is 'every person who drives or is in actual physical control of a vehicle' (DEF-NRS-484A-080), read through the vehicle's controlled motion. 'Passenger vehicle' has no posted definition: it is read as a vehicle (the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) not built to carry goods or to be drawn: not ru.truck ('motor vehicle for carrying goods, with a body built for that purpose') and not ru.trailer_or_combination ('vehicle drawn by another, or the combination'), carried beside the aggregate."}, {"span": "s9", "atoms": [], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "'While actually engaged in' fixes the loading to the stop itself: the door of s11 is open at an observation of the same halt (drv.motion.complete_halt, 'at rest at the observation'); the purpose is read by that conduct."}, {"span": "s11", "atoms": ["sig.door_open"], "derived": [], "justification": "The loading or unloading of passengers is read by the act through which passengers board or alight: a door of the vehicle open (sig.door_open, 'a door open; side in {traffic, curb}')."}, {"span": "s13", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-030::bus", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-270::taxicab"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Any bus or taxicab': the admitted aggregates DEF-NRS-484A-030::bus and DEF-NRS-484A-270::taxicab, each claimed as one atom."}, {"span": "s14", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.curb_zone", "st.region_geometry"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "'Waiting to enter or about to enter such zone' is read by the conduct: the bus or taxicab does not overlap the zone the subject occupies (rel.occupies, st.curb_zone) and is halted (drv.motion.complete_halt) with the ground distance from its body to the zone (st.region_geometry, 'the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it') within p.zone_entry_wait_reach."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "s8", "standard": "temporarily", "concepts": ["drv.motion.parked"], "params": ["p.standing_min_duration", "p.halt_speed_tolerance"], "convention": "curbside passenger pick-up dwell: a stop counts as temporary while it has not lasted as long as a passenger pick-up dwell, i.e. while the subject is not at rest at every observation of a window of length p.standing_min_duration behind the observation (drv.motion.parked)", "surrogate": false}, {"span": "s10", "standard": "expeditiously", "concepts": ["drv.motion.parked"], "params": ["p.standing_min_duration", "p.halt_speed_tolerance"], "convention": "curbside passenger pick-up dwell: loading or unloading counts as expeditious while the halt has not lasted as long as a passenger pick-up dwell (drv.motion.parked with min_duration p.standing_min_duration); the same bound as the temporary stop it qualifies", "surrogate": false}, {"span": "s12", "standard": "does not interfere with", "concepts": ["drv.motion.complete_halt", "st.region_geometry", "rel.occupies"], "params": ["p.zone_entry_wait_reach", "p.halt_speed_tolerance"], "convention": "queueing at a curb space: a stop interferes with a bus or taxicab where, at some observation of the stop so far, it stands halted outside the zone within one passenger-car length plus a queue spacing of it (p.zone_entry_wait_reach), the place a vehicle waits to take the space", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) whose footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) a curb zone z (st.curb_zone) that is of kind bus_stop while the subject is not a bus (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-030::bus false), or of kind taxicab_stand while the subject is not a taxicab (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-270::taxicab false).", "obligation": "Wherever the subject occupies such a zone z (selected again as in the applicability, with its kind and the subject's class), the subject is not halted (drv.motion.complete_halt with p.halt_speed_tolerance), except a halt that is (a) to avoid conflict with other traffic: some other road user is ahead of the subject in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) with a gap between bodies (rel.surface_gap) at most p.queue_halt_gap; or (b) in compliance with a device or an officer: a travel region the subject occupies is governed (dev.governs) by a stop sign, a yield sign, a traffic signal displaying a red or yellow indication or flashing_red, a railway signal or gate with lights flashing or gate not up, or a person in the role police_officer giving the indication stop; or (c) a temporary, expeditious stop of a passenger vehicle for passengers: the subject is neither a truck (ru.truck) nor a trailer or combination (ru.trailer_or_combination), it is not parked with min_duration p.standing_min_duration (drv.motion.parked), a door of the subject is open (sig.door_open) at some observation of the same halt, before or after the observation, and at no observation of the halt up to the judged one is there a road user other than the subject that is a bus or a taxicab (the two admitted aggregates), whose footprint does not overlap z, which is halted (drv.motion.complete_halt), and whose body's ground distance to z (st.region_geometry) is at most p.zone_entry_wait_reach.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance", "p.queue_halt_gap", "p.standing_min_duration", "p.zone_entry_wait_reach"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "'A person shall not stop, stand or park a vehicle' is read on the vehicle's controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s7", "why": "'The driver of a passenger vehicle' is read on the vehicle's controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s6", "why": "Official designation and appropriate signing are read from the presence of the curb zone of kind bus_stop or taxicab_stand on the road.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s9", "why": "The purpose of loading or unloading passengers is read by a door of the halted vehicle open during the halt.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "purpose"}, {"span": "s14", "why": "'Waiting to enter or about to enter' is read by a bus or taxicab halted outside the zone within the waiting reach; one still moving toward the zone is not read as waiting.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "intention"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A passenger car halts in a bus_stop curb zone for longer than the standing duration, doors closed; no road user ahead and no stop control governs its lane."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A passenger car halts briefly in a bus_stop curb zone with its curb-side door open and moves off before the standing duration; no other road user is in the scene."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A bus halts in a bus_stop curb zone."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "A passenger car halts briefly in a taxicab_stand curb zone and the source does not observe its doors.", "masked": ["sig.door_open"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A passenger car halts briefly in a bus_stop zone with a door open while a bus stands halted just outside the zone within the waiting reach."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A truck halts briefly in a taxicab_stand zone with a door open: it is no passenger vehicle."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition source (sensor or simulator specification)"}, {"name": "p.queue_halt_gap", "unit": "m", "value": 5.0, "convention": "the gap between bodies to a road user ahead in the same lane within which a halt is a halt behind other traffic: the spacing of halted vehicles in a queue", "source": "HCM queue spacing of stopped vehicles"}, {"name": "p.standing_min_duration", "unit": "s", "value": 60.0, "convention": "the longest halt counted as receiving or discharging passengers or loading rather than standing: a passenger pick-up dwell at the curb", "source": "curbside passenger pick-up dwell observations (ITE curbside management practice)"}, {"name": "p.zone_entry_wait_reach", "unit": "m", "value": 10.0, "convention": "the ground distance from a halted vehicle's body to a curb zone within which the vehicle counts as waiting to enter the zone: about one design passenger-car length plus the spacing of halted vehicles in a queue", "source": "AASHTO Green Book design vehicle dimensions; HCM queue spacing"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_533", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-533"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "A vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "shall not be permitted to stand", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "unattended", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "upon any perceptible grade", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "without stopping the engine and effectively setting the brake thereon and turning the front wheels to the curb or side of the highway.", "role": "obligation"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle ('every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway, except ...'), claimed as one atom."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": [], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "'Stand' is 'the halting of a vehicle, whether occupied or not, otherwise than for the purpose of and while actually engaged in receiving or discharging passengers' (DEF-NRS-484A-250): a halt, drv.motion.complete_halt ('at rest at the observation ... its speed at or below a tolerance', p.halt_speed_tolerance). The definition's exclusion of passenger receiving is not carried: the duty reads only a vehicle with no person in it (s3), which no passenger is being received into while it stays so. 'Shall not be permitted' is read on the vehicle's conduct, whoever is in charge of it."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["ru.occupant_count"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Unattended': no person is in or on the vehicle to attend it, ru.occupant_count, 'the number of persons in or on a vehicle (an integer attribute of a road user)', equal to none. A source that observes arrivals but not a total declares it absent, and the rule is then unknown."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["st.grade", "rel.occupies", "st.highway"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Upon any perceptible grade': the subject is on a highway (rel.occupies; st.highway, 'the entire public way between its boundary lines', which the words' 'side of the highway' names) at a place whose slope (st.grade, 'longitudinal slope of the roadway at a point'; not a stand-in for the place of a crest, which is not read) stands clear of zero: its magnitude exceeds p.grade_resolution. The words name the grade's presence, not a size: 'perceptible' is read as a slope the source resolves."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": ["kin.engine_running", "kin.parking_brake", "kin.steer_angle", "prim.region_lateral_offset", "st.road_edge", "st.on_way", "st.highway"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Stopping the engine': kin.engine_running, 'the vehicle's engine or motor is running, so that propulsion is available', must be false; it is 'not a stand-in for motion or a halt', and the halt is read separately (s2). 'Setting the brake thereon' on an unattended vehicle is the parking brake: kin.parking_brake, 'the parking brake (hand brake) is set'; not a stand-in for the service brake or the brake lamp, neither of which is read, since no person presses a pedal in an unattended vehicle. 'Turning the front wheels to the curb or side of the highway': kin.steer_angle, 'front-wheel steering angle' (not a stand-in for a path or a manoeuvre, and it is read as the wheels' position only), turned beyond p.steer_angle_resolution toward the side on which the nearest curb or edge lies. The curb or side is the road edge (st.road_edge, 'curb or edge of the roadway') lying on the subject's highway (st.on_way, 'the public way a structure region lies on'; st.highway) nearest the subject, and its side is the sign of its lateral offset (prim.region_lateral_offset, 'the signed lateral offset (m, left positive) of a structure region from a road user ... perpendicular to the road user's heading')."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) that is halted (drv.motion.complete_halt with p.halt_speed_tolerance), with no person in or on it (ru.occupant_count equal to none), whose footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) a highway h (st.highway), and the magnitude of the grade at its place (st.grade) exceeds p.grade_resolution.", "obligation": "At every observation at which the applicability holds, with h selected again as there: the engine is not running (kin.engine_running false); the parking brake is set (kin.parking_brake); and the front wheels are turned toward the curb or side: of the road edges (st.road_edge) lying on h (st.on_way), the one with the smallest absolute lateral offset from the subject (prim.region_lateral_offset) gives the side, and the steering angle (kin.steer_angle) exceeds p.steer_angle_resolution in magnitude and has the sign of that offset, both read left-positive.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance", "p.grade_resolution", "p.steer_angle_resolution"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s2", "why": "'Shall not be permitted to stand' is read on the vehicle's conduct: the duty binds the standing vehicle whoever is in charge of it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "'Effectively setting the brake' is read as the parking brake set while the vehicle stays at rest; the brake's holding force is not observed.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "The curb or side of the highway is read as the road edge nearest the vehicle, and the steering angle's sign is read left-positive, as kin.yaw_rate and prim.region_lateral_offset are; the direction the wheels should point for an uphill or downhill grade is not distinguished, the words not distinguishing it.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car stands with no one in it on a clearly sloped street, its engine running, parking brake set, wheels turned toward the nearest curb."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A car stands with no one in it on the same slope, engine off, parking brake set, front wheels turned toward the right-hand curb, which is the nearest road edge."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A car stands with no one in it on a level street, its grade within the resolution."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in permit, but the source does not observe the parking brake.", "masked": ["kin.parking_brake"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car stands unattended on the slope, engine off, parking brake set, front wheels straight."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A car stands on the slope with its driver inside."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition source (sensor or simulator specification)"}, {"name": "p.grade_resolution", "unit": "ratio", "value": 0.005, "convention": "the longitudinal slope at or below which a roadway reads as level: the grade resolution of map elevation profiles", "source": "HD-map elevation profile accuracy specifications"}, {"name": "p.steer_angle_resolution", "unit": "deg", "value": 2.0, "convention": "the front-wheel steering angle at or below which a parked vehicle's wheels read as straight: the steering-angle sensor resolution plus the play of a parked vehicle's wheels", "source": "steering-angle sensor specifications (SAE J670 vehicle dynamics terminology)"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_557_o1", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-557"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "The Department of Transportation, and local authorities with the approval of the Department of Transportation, may designate dangerous highway grade crossings of railroads", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "and erect official traffic-control devices at such crossings directing a stop.", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "When such stop signs are erected", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "the driver of any vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "shall stop within 50 feet but not less than 15 feet from the nearest track of such a grade crossing", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s7", "text": "and afterward may proceed only", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s8", "text": "upon exercising due care.", "role": "sibling"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["st.railway_crossing", "st.on_way", "st.highway"], "derived": [], "justification": "A 'highway grade crossing of a railroad' ('railroad' is 'a carrier of persons or property upon cars ... operated upon stationary rails', DEF-NRS-484A-200) is st.railway_crossing, 'level crossing of a railway with the roadway, and its nearest rail', lying on a highway (st.on_way, 'the public way a structure region lies on'; st.highway). The authority's designation of it as dangerous is its legal status, evidenced by the stop sign erected for it (s2, s3)."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["dev.stop_sign"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Official traffic-control devices ... directing a stop' ('every sign, signal, marking and device ... placed or erected by a public authority or railroad', DEF-NRS-484A-145) are stop signs: dev.stop_sign, 'regulatory sign requiring a full halt'; its presence is the evidence that it is official."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["dev.governs", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "'When such stop signs are erected': the stop sign governs (dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls'; not a stand-in for a position, and the place of the halt is read from the crossing, not from the sign) a travel region (st.travel_region) the subject occupies (rel.occupies) on its approach, and that region lies on the same highway as the crossing (st.on_way): the chain of relations ties the sign to 'such crossings'."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Driver' is 'every person who drives or is in actual physical control of a vehicle' (DEF-NRS-484A-080), a role read through the vehicle's controlled motion; 'any vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": ["st.region_geometry", "rel.occupies", "st.railway_crossing"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "'Stop' when required means 'complete cessation from movement' (DEF-NRS-484A-255, whose own scope 'when required' these words meet): drv.motion.complete_halt, whose contract quotes it, with p.halt_speed_tolerance. The place of the halt: the ground distance from the subject's body to the crossing (st.region_geometry, 'the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it (zero when they overlap)'), the crossing being st.railway_crossing with 'its nearest rail', is at most the upper and at least the lower figure the span states (literals), and the subject's footprint does not yet overlap the crossing (rel.occupies). 'Such a grade crossing' is the crossing s1 to s3 select, re-bound with every relation that fixed it."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle), and the judged observation is an entry of the subject into a railway crossing x (st.railway_crossing): its footprint overlaps x (rel.occupies) and did not at the previous observation, and at that previous observation the subject occupied a travel region r (st.travel_region) governed (dev.governs) by a stop sign (dev.stop_sign), where r and x lie on the same highway h (st.on_way, st.highway).", "obligation": "Duty of an act before an event (rule 4c). Event: the entry of the applicability, for the crossing x and the governed region r it selects. Act and place: at some observation of the search the subject is halted (drv.motion.complete_halt with p.halt_speed_tolerance), its footprint does not overlap x (rel.occupies), and the ground distance from its body to x (st.region_geometry) is at most the upper literal of s5 and at least its lower literal. Search: back from the observation before the entry, through observations at which the subject does not overlap x and its distance to x is at most the upper literal (the stopping zone). History bound: the search ends at the approach start, the last observation before the entry at which the subject does not overlap x and its distance to x exceeds the upper literal, or at the subject's previous exit from x (the observation at which it ceased to overlap x), the previous occurrence of the same event; nothing else ends it, not the start of the recording nor a first observation. Verdict: where the search finds the halt, the duty is met; where it reaches either end without the halt, the duty is violated; where it reaches the subject's first observation, inside the zone, with neither end found and no halt, the duty is unknown. A distance, an overlap or a speed unobserved at an observation of the search makes the search unknown from that point unless a halt in the zone was found nearer the entry. Whether the entry occurred is unknown where the previous observation does not show the subject's overlap with x, and whether the stop sign governs is unknown where governance of r is not observed.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s4", "why": "'The driver of any vehicle' is read on the vehicle's controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s1", "why": "The designation of the crossing as dangerous by the Department or a local authority is read from the presence of a stop sign governing the approach to the crossing.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s2", "why": "That the device is official and directs a stop is read from the presence of a stop sign.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s3", "why": "A stop sign governing a travel region on the same highway as the crossing, occupied on the approach to the entry, is read as the sign erected at that crossing; the sign's own position is not read.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "s6", "why": "The distance 'from the nearest track' is read as the distance from the vehicle's body to the crossing region, whose near boundary is its nearest rail.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car on a lane governed by a stop sign approaches a railway crossing on the same highway from beyond the upper figure and drives into it without halting."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The car halts at a distance from the crossing between the two figures, then drives into it."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The car drives into a railway crossing from a lane that no stop sign governs."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The car halts somewhere on its approach and then enters the crossing, but the source maps no region outlines, so its distance to the crossing is unknown at every observation.", "masked": ["st.region_geometry"]}, {"name": "history_boundary", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The recording begins with the car already moving inside the stopping zone, between the two figures from the crossing; it enters the crossing without a recorded halt; a halt before the recording cannot be excluded.", "boundary": "the car's approach from the observation at which it was last farther than the upper figure from the crossing up to the start of the recording"}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "The car halts only closer to the crossing than the lower figure, then enters it."}], "literals": [{"span": "s5", "text": "50 feet", "value": 50, "unit": "ft"}, {"span": "s5", "text": "15 feet", "value": 15, "unit": "ft"}], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition source (sensor or simulator specification)"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_557_o2", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-557"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "The Department of Transportation, and local authorities with the approval of the Department of Transportation, may designate dangerous highway grade crossings of railroads", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "and erect official traffic-control devices at such crossings directing a stop.", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "When such stop signs are erected", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "the driver of any vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "shall stop within 50 feet but not less than 15 feet from the nearest track of such a grade crossing", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s7", "text": "and afterward may proceed only", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s8", "text": "upon exercising due care.", "role": "standard"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["st.railway_crossing", "st.on_way", "st.highway"], "derived": [], "justification": "A 'highway grade crossing of a railroad' ('railroad' is 'a carrier of persons or property upon cars ... operated upon stationary rails', DEF-NRS-484A-200) is st.railway_crossing, 'level crossing of a railway with the roadway, and its nearest rail', lying on a highway (st.on_way, 'the public way a structure region lies on'; st.highway). The authority's designation of it as dangerous is evidenced by the stop sign erected for it."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["dev.stop_sign"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Official traffic-control devices ... directing a stop' (DEF-NRS-484A-145) are stop signs: dev.stop_sign, 'regulatory sign requiring a full halt'; its presence is the evidence that it is official."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["dev.governs", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "'When such stop signs are erected': the stop sign governs (dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls'; not a stand-in for a position) a travel region (st.travel_region) the subject occupies (rel.occupies) on its approach, lying on the same highway as the crossing (st.on_way)."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Driver' is 'every person who drives or is in actual physical control of a vehicle' (DEF-NRS-484A-080), read through the vehicle's controlled motion; 'any vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": ["st.region_geometry", "rel.occupies", "st.railway_crossing"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "'Afterward' refers to the stop: 'complete cessation from movement' (DEF-NRS-484A-255), drv.motion.complete_halt, whose contract quotes it, with p.halt_speed_tolerance. The referent is carried in full: the halt itself, at the place the span states, not compliance with the stop rule. The place of that halt: the ground distance from the subject's body to the crossing (st.region_geometry, 'the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it'), st.railway_crossing with 'its nearest rail', between the lower and the upper figure the span states (literals), the footprint not yet overlapping the crossing (rel.occupies)."}, {"span": "s7", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.railway_crossing"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Proceed' after the halt is the subject's entry into the crossing: its footprint comes to overlap (rel.occupies, 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region') the railway crossing (st.railway_crossing), and the duty runs while it occupies it."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "s8", "standard": "due care", "concepts": ["prim.closest_approach_within", "prim.closest_approach_distance", "rel.contact", "ru.rail_vehicle"], "params": ["p.conflict_horizon", "p.conflict_centre_clearance"], "convention": "traffic-conflict technique: proceeding across the crossing with due care is read by its outcome: from the entry and while the vehicle occupies the crossing, no rail vehicle (ru.rail_vehicle) approaches it within the conflict horizon (prim.closest_approach_within with p.conflict_horizon) to a centre distance below the collision clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance below p.conflict_centre_clearance), and the vehicle's body touches no road user (rel.contact)", "surrogate": true}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) that has entered a railway crossing x (st.railway_crossing; its footprint overlaps x and did not at the previous observation) from a travel region r (st.travel_region) it occupied at the previous observation, governed (dev.governs) by a stop sign (dev.stop_sign), r and x lying on the same highway h (st.on_way, st.highway), and afterward: on that approach, searched back from the observation before the entry to the last observation at which it was farther than the upper literal of s5 from x or to its previous exit from x, it was halted (drv.motion.complete_halt with p.halt_speed_tolerance) at an observation at which it did not overlap x and its body's ground distance to x (st.region_geometry) lay between the lower and the upper literal of s5. The applicability holds at that entry and at every later observation while the subject occupies x without having left it; it is unknown where the search reaches the subject's first observation without a halt or either end.", "obligation": "At every observation at which the applicability holds: no rail vehicle (ru.rail_vehicle) has a closest approach to the subject within p.conflict_horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) at a centre distance below p.conflict_centre_clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance), and the subject is in contact (rel.contact) with no road user.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance", "p.conflict_horizon", "p.conflict_centre_clearance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s4", "why": "'The driver of any vehicle' is read on the vehicle's controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s1", "why": "The designation of the crossing as dangerous is read from the presence of a stop sign governing the approach to it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s2", "why": "That the device is official and directs a stop is read from the presence of a stop sign.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s8", "why": "Due care, a standard about the driver's state of mind, is read only through the outcome of the crossing: no conflict with a rail vehicle and no contact with any road user while on the crossing; the rule is a surrogate and its verdicts are evidence, not a legal conclusion.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car on a lane governed by a stop sign halts between the two figures from the crossing, then enters it while a train closes on it so that their closest approach within the conflict horizon lies below the clearance."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The car halts between the two figures, then enters and clears the crossing; no other road user is in the scene."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The car enters a railway crossing from a lane that no stop sign governs."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The car halts between the two figures and enters the crossing; no train is present, a pedestrian stands on the crossing near its path, and the source does not observe contact.", "masked": ["rel.contact"]}], "literals": [{"span": "s5", "text": "50 feet", "value": 50, "unit": "ft"}, {"span": "s5", "text": "15 feet", "value": 15, "unit": "ft"}], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition source (sensor or simulator specification)"}, {"name": "p.conflict_horizon", "unit": "s", "value": 3.0, "convention": "time-to-collision threshold of the traffic-conflict technique: a closest approach later than this is not a present danger of a crash", "source": "Hyden, The Swedish Traffic Conflict Technique (1987)"}, {"name": "p.conflict_centre_clearance", "unit": "m", "value": 3.0, "convention": "centre-to-centre distance at the closest approach below which the bodies of a passenger car and another road user are taken to collide or nearly collide: about a car's half-length plus half a body width", "source": "AASHTO Green Book design passenger car dimensions"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
